      <item>
        <title>RT by @elonmusk: Starlink enables fast, reliable connectivity where traditional infrastructure does not exist 🛰️🏔️</title>
        <dc:creator>@Starlink</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>Starlink enables fast, reliable connectivity where traditional infrastructure does not exist 🛰️🏔️</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>OffRoadCampingBoys (@OffRoadCampBoys)</b>
<p>
<p>Many of the areas we went, there is not a single cell provider that has reception for long distances.  Here is a speed test location at one camp site. And, yes, the more remote the better it performs.  We ran Starlink for 8,431 miles - non-stop and turned off cellular data to prevent switching and dropping from the network.</p>
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHNosb2dXkAAT--w.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />

<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHNoscP5XQAAXsnN.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/OffRoadCampBoys/status/2079023053942751663#m">https://nitter.net/OffRoadCampBoys/status/2079023053942751663#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
